  "title": "MySQL: Correct case when zlib and zstd flags are both set",
  "description": "There are two flags in the \"Login Request\" for compression:\n\n`mysql.caps.cp`\n![image](/uploads/fec41a68fec65d0d5068cca47284ffb6/image.png)\n\n`mysql.caps.compress_zsd`\n![image](/uploads/9156574976d5adb9fc893221330290c9/image.png)\n\nIf both are set then zlib is used, not zstd.\n\nNote that small packets have a uncompressed payload and are identical if either of the two flags are set.\n\nLarger packets with `mysql.compressed_packet_length_uncompressed >0` are actually compressed with zlib or zstd.\n\nExample pcap:\n\n[mysql_zlib_zstd.pcapng](/uploads/98a92b516713c33b53442f7ba46085d8/mysql_zlib_zstd.pcapng)",
